  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 6.3: \"Average Subsidy Progression for 100 Agents\", one curve per signal strength. The curves separate by how long the subsidy has to keep paying. At signal strength 0.99 (yellow) and 0.9 (magenta) the subsidy is at or near zero throughout. At 0.8 (cyan) it spikes early and is gone by about agent 18; at 0.7 (red) it peaks near 0.07 at about agent 4 and decays to zero by about agent 60; at 0.6 (green) it peaks near 0.062 around agent 8 and is still decaying, at about 0.003, at agent 100. At 0.51 (blue) it behaves differently in kind — it RISES to about 0.022 by agent 40 and then stays flat to agent 100 rather than decaying. The weakest signal is the one where the subsidy never stops being needed.",
